WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.606
Module 5: waves, Culture
Dig and presenting findings.

00:00:03.606 --> 00:00:08.776
In about thirty minutes you'll learn to
run a second wave that can fairly be

00:00:08.776 --> 00:00:11.702
compared with the first,
read what changed,

00:00:11.702 --> 00:00:14.967
see how Mosaic Signal
feeds a Culture Dig score,

00:00:14.967 --> 00:00:18.573
and present findings that
hold up to tough questions.

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:22.494
An extra wave runs the same
framework again later.

00:00:22.494 --> 00:00:26.950
You can buy up to three, with the
launch or later from Purchases.

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:30.926
To start one, press "Start wave
two" on the launch's card.

00:00:30.926 --> 00:00:36.273
SurveyCraft copies the launch survey as
you last edited it, with no responses,

00:00:36.273 --> 00:00:37.506
into a new survey.

00:00:37.506 --> 00:00:41.688
It gets the same respondent cap,
and its own launch deadline,

00:00:41.688 --> 00:00:43.813
about two months from that day.

00:00:43.813 --> 00:00:45.115
Two things to know.

00:00:45.115 --> 00:00:48.954
Waves are separate surveys,
each with its own analytics,

00:00:48.954 --> 00:00:52.039
and SurveyCraft doesn't
overlay them for you.

00:00:52.039 --> 00:00:57.523
And the launch's card on Purchases lists
every wave, with a link to open it and,

00:00:57.523 --> 00:00:59.922
once it's live, to see its results.

00:01:00.433 --> 00:01:03.914
A comparison is only as fair
as what you held steady.

00:01:03.914 --> 00:01:09.102
Keep the questions about the story word
for word, and keep the prompt the same.

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:12.780
Remember that the wave copies
the launch as last edited,

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.670
so don't tidy up the
launch after it closes.

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:19.545
Keep the audience, channels
and season as close as you can.

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:24.076
If you must change something, change
the wave's copy, not the launch,

00:01:24.076 --> 00:01:28.739
leave the questions about the story
alone, and write down what changed.

00:01:28.739 --> 00:01:34.190
And time the wave for when people have
lived through the change long enough to have

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:35.307
stories about it.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:39.902
Northwind ran wave 2 in September,
with the same questions.

00:01:39.902 --> 00:01:45.604
A hundred and eighteen stories came in,
mostly through the new cross-site huddles.

00:01:45.604 --> 00:01:46.786
The shapes moved.

00:01:46.786 --> 00:01:52.348
Stories near Able went from nine of a
hundred and forty-two to twenty-seven of a

00:01:52.348 --> 00:01:53.809
hundred and eighteen.

00:01:53.809 --> 00:01:59.302
Stories at the word-of-mouth end of the
channel slider fell from fifty-eight to

00:01:59.302 --> 00:02:03.891
twenty-six, and among clinic stories,
from thirty-six to fourteen.

00:02:03.891 --> 00:02:07.367
Resources and clinic support
moved toward present.

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:12.721
Now choose the best summary, and watch
for the caution about where wave 2 was

00:02:12.721 --> 00:02:13.416
collected.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:19.416
Standalone Mosaic Signal doesn't test
change for you, so judge it carefully.

00:02:19.416 --> 00:02:24.643
Compare shapes and the number of
stories in a region, not just averages.

00:02:24.643 --> 00:02:26.385
Then ask four questions.

00:02:26.385 --> 00:02:28.054
Who answered this time?

00:02:28.054 --> 00:02:30.159
Is the shift big and visible?

00:02:30.159 --> 00:02:31.683
Do the stories agree?

00:02:31.683 --> 00:02:33.861
And does other evidence agree?

00:02:33.861 --> 00:02:36.256
Sometimes tools seem to disagree.

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:42.208
Northwind's progress check in October showed
no meaningful change in Change Ready,

00:02:42.208 --> 00:02:44.604
while the Signal stories shifted.

00:02:44.604 --> 00:02:45.838
Both can be true.

00:02:45.838 --> 00:02:51.572
The stories are about how specific changes
landed for nursing and clinic staff.

00:02:51.572 --> 00:02:56.290
The tile measures broader readiness
across everyone who answered.

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:59.484
Report both, and say
what each one measures.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.646
You met Culture Dig in the Mosaic course,

00:03:02.646 --> 00:03:06.583
and the Culture Dig certification
covers running the program.

00:03:06.583 --> 00:03:09.875
Here's what matters about
the instrument inside it.

00:03:09.875 --> 00:03:13.166
A dig's story collection
is a Mosaic Signal survey,

00:03:13.166 --> 00:03:17.039
given questions with fixed
directions so they can be scored.

00:03:17.039 --> 00:03:19.427
Look at how the composite reads them.

00:03:19.427 --> 00:03:23.687
The slider input is the average
position toward the healthier end.

00:03:23.687 --> 00:03:28.205
The triad input is the average weight
away from the concerning corner.

00:03:28.205 --> 00:03:32.723
And the stones input is the share of
placements in the healthy corner.

00:03:32.723 --> 00:03:37.950
Two of those three are averages, so the
composite inherits the averaging problem.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:43.243
A domain split into two camps can score
the same as one where everyone sits in the

00:03:43.243 --> 00:03:43.695
middle.

00:03:43.695 --> 00:03:46.341
That's why the dig report draws the dots,

00:03:46.341 --> 00:03:49.374
and won't draw them for
fewer than ten stories,

00:03:49.374 --> 00:03:51.827
because a scatter can identify people.

00:03:52.333 --> 00:03:57.040
There's no deck to hand over, so
you build the story of the stories.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:00.570
Start with the question
and who told their stories.

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:05.484
Then three to five patterns, each
from a Pattern Card: the chart first,

00:04:05.484 --> 00:04:06.869
then a story or two.

00:04:06.869 --> 00:04:10.675
Then group differences, only
for groups of ten or more.

00:04:10.675 --> 00:04:13.721
Then bright spots and
outliers, as examples.

00:04:13.721 --> 00:04:19.120
Then honest limits: stories, not staff,
no score, no benchmark, relationships,

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:19.881
not causes.

00:04:19.881 --> 00:04:22.027
Then options and the next wave.

00:04:22.027 --> 00:04:24.380
Say it in the storytellers' words.

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:27.772
If the client wants an
outside voice in the room,

00:04:27.772 --> 00:04:32.686
the readout add-on is a ninety-minute
session with a Mosaic consultant.

00:04:32.686 --> 00:04:37.185
And share the findings back with
the people who told the stories.

00:04:37.185 --> 00:04:41.130
It's the best reason for them
to tell you more next time.

00:04:41.633 --> 00:04:45.545
You're presenting the decisions
study to Northwind's executives.

00:04:45.545 --> 00:04:47.929
Choose the best reply to each question.

00:04:48.433 --> 00:04:53.038
Coaches can deploy a Mosaic Signal
study from Mosaic Coaching Studio,

00:04:53.038 --> 00:04:55.774
but only in tenants with Mosaic included.

00:04:55.774 --> 00:05:01.112
The coach picks a framework, names the
study and says how many people to expect.

00:05:01.112 --> 00:05:03.314
The study starts as the template,

00:05:03.314 --> 00:05:07.718
with the same cap and deadline as
a bought launch, and no add-ons.

00:05:07.718 --> 00:05:12.389
There's no generated report: the card
says "Report not available yet".

00:05:12.389 --> 00:05:15.525
The charts and stories
are read in SurveyCraft,

00:05:15.525 --> 00:05:20.263
where the coach is set up as a user
under the email they deployed with.

00:05:20.263 --> 00:05:22.732
Editing the prompt happens there too.

00:05:23.233 --> 00:05:28.057
Here's your Readout Outline, with
phrases that work and phrases to avoid.

00:05:28.057 --> 00:05:28.850
Download it.

00:05:29.333 --> 00:05:32.912
Now the module check: five
questions, four to pass.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:34.069
To recap.

00:05:34.069 --> 00:05:39.276
An extra wave copies the launch as
last edited, with its own deadline,

00:05:39.276 --> 00:05:40.837
as a separate survey.

00:05:40.837 --> 00:05:43.589
Hold the questions and prompt steady.

00:05:43.589 --> 00:05:47.308
Compare shapes and story
counts, ask who answered,

00:05:47.308 --> 00:05:51.473
and reconcile with other tools
without picking a winner.

00:05:51.473 --> 00:05:55.786
Inside Culture Dig, look at
the dots behind the composite.

00:05:55.786 --> 00:06:01.513
And present patterns, counts and stories,
never scores, benchmarks or causes.

00:06:01.513 --> 00:06:03.075
Next, your practical.
